@*
    Our Values (2026-08-03) — docs/03_PageBlueprints.md "Page — Our Values".
    Title/description/canonical/OG/AboutPage schema come from
    ViewData["Seo"] + ViewData["SeoPageType"], set in ValuesController.Index
    via ISeoService — see _Layout.cshtml's <head> and
    SeoStructuredDataViewComponent.

    Folkart-reference revision (2026-08-16, project owner-approved) — page
    flow rebuilt to follow the supplied Folkart "Değerlerimiz" screenshot's
    layout: Breadcrumb → plain page heading (no Hero Banner) → Introduction
    → Core Values → Footer. Same pattern as About/Index.cshtml's own
    Folkart-reference revision (2026-08-13). HeroBannerStandard and
    QualityCommitmentViewComponent are intentionally not invoked here — the
    project owner asked for no hero area and no section beyond the value
    items on this page. Neither component nor its assets were modified or
    deleted; both are simply unused by this page now.

    Project owner's 2026-08-16 decision: the reference's four value
    headings (İnsan Merkezli Yaklaşım / İnovasyon / Çeşitlilik / Fayda) do
    not correspond to this site's six existing values (Güven / Kalite /
    Şeffaflık / Sürdürülebilirlik / Yenilikçilik / Müşteri Odaklılık), so
    the six existing headings/copy are kept as-is — only the presentation
    (plain underlined heading + full-width paragraph, no cards/icons)
    follows the reference. See CoreValuesViewComponent.
*@

@{
    var breadcrumbTrail = new List<AncinInsaat.ViewComponents.BreadcrumbItem>
    {
        new() { Label = "Değerlerimiz" }
    };
}
@await Component.InvokeAsync("Breadcrumb", new { trail = breadcrumbTrail, homeLabel = "Anasayfa" })

<section class="section values-heading-section">
    <div class="container">
        <h1 id="values-heading" class="values-heading">Değerlerimiz</h1>
    </div>
</section>

@await Component.InvokeAsync("ValuesIntroduction")

@await Component.InvokeAsync("CoreValues")
